{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal","id":320767,"title":"I see Dead Peop...I mean the Future: About High Awareness Sidereal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-24T08:47:08-08:00","id":320767,"title":"I see Dead Peop...I mean the Future: About High Awareness Sidereal","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/RuSqgLO.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">~ Heh...hehhehheh....AHHHAAHAHAHA..KIIHIHIHIHIHIH... ..Hope you like Someone Else's Destiny you little monkey ~</span></div> <br /> Ummm, delicious Prior Warning making assassins cries like little babies. But wait, does this mean it's impossible to gank a paranoid Sidereal with high Per + Awareness who constantly commit motes to this charm 24/7 ? Since I'm planning to make a Sidereal like that and I would like to know how to create problems for her, kinda hard when she keep alert the 4 combat-monkey in the Circle to put-up all of their Scene-long charm and then proceed to curb-storm every enemies who try to ambush her....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:04:27-08:00","id":320791,"title":"","content":"Prior Warning isn't really the problem - that one gives you a general idea that something bad is about to happen a few minutes in advance, but doesn't specify what the danger is. You can get around this by making it so that whatever the danger is either of a kind that the characters are not expecting (poison gas attack when they expect armed thugs, fire when they are expecting poison, pit full of spikes when they expect fire), or that the amount of time they have to prepare is not enough. Also, splitting the party to prevent the Awareness Sid from alerting his buddies would fix several problems.<br /> <br /> Expected Pain is worse. That one makes you effectively immune to surprise, mechanically speaking. Again, though, my solution would be to make it so &quot;an instant&quot; is not enough warning time. For example, Expected Pain might alert you to the group of thugs that is about to ambush you, but it doesn't really matter because they'll be there in less than five ticks and your only escape route got locked down ten minutes earlier.<br /> <br /> Now, if your Sidereal has Prior Warning, Expected Pain, AND Avoidance Kata, there may simply be nothing you can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-24-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:26:34-08:00","id":320798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320791#post320791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if your Sidereal has Prior Warning, Expected Pain, AND Avoidance Kata, there may simply be nothing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are still some things to be done for Avoidance Kata. If a Sidereal's in a position where suddenly being somewhere else runs really counter to that Sidereal's goals and wants (e.g. &quot;This noncombatant I'm in love with will be killed if I'm not here to help!&quot; or &quot;Man, that city sure is going to be a smoking crater unless I stop this superweapon from being activated!&quot; ), that's a potentially very high price the Sidereal pays to use it, and one that has little-to-nothing to do with mechanics. There's also that I believe the ST decides where the Sidereal winds up instead; the new situation may also not be the most desired position in the world. For more on Avoidance Kata, see <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/avoidance-kata\" target=\"_blank\">these notes</a> on Chancel Aleph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:28:55-08:00","id":320800,"title":"","content":"It might depend on who and what you are.<br /> <br /> For instance, it seems to have been part of Jenna Moran's process that Solars could develop custom Charms that would have novel ways to get around or keep up with Sidereal tricks.<br /> <br /> Some of the developer comments on the Charm design seems to be following this logic and front running it; they're already speculating on the things Sidereals can do so they can design Charms representing Solars countering them, perhaps.<br /> <br /> If you're a regular person, and you've not been equipped by, say, demons or something, then yeah, you're probably not really equipped to overcome Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:33:22-08:00","id":320876,"title":"","content":"Awareness also contains the rediculous Wise Choice charm. For a small cost, you can know which choice (of any finite set you list) will lead to the best personal outcome for you! This has some obvious Paranoia uses: which path home should I take, should I get in the first carriage or the second one, should I trust Vizier Judas Starscream or not, etc. It can also be used to predict exactly who is going to try to assassinate you next (most useful if you know someone is gunning for you). Have a friend set up a betting pool, where people can guess names and whoever guesses right gets a prize. Then, get a bunch of tiles with letters on them, and assemble a name using Wise Choice (which tile should I place on the board next, given that I'm going to keep doing this until I get a complete name?) and then enter the result into the betting pool. Since the best outcome for you is both a) winning the bet and b) finding the assassin, the charm will give you the correct answer every time (barring cases where knowing your would-be killer is worse for you than not knowing, in which case you should be fine not knowing). Of course, this is an incredibly ineficient O(n) method that would drain motes like crazy, and only works for within the next month unless you exploit recursion, but I think optimizing information gains from Wise Choice is slightly outside the scope of this post.<br /> <br /> As a side note, you would be amazed at how much you can get done with Wise Choice and a grid map of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:37:12-08:00","id":320879,"title":"","content":"Finding a way to threaten something that a given Sidereal will actually stay and fight for has traditionally been a good way of short-circuiting a lot of their tricks. Who cares if you can sense future danger or declare yourself absent from fights when I have my daiklave's edge to the throat of your wife/son/secretary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T12:58:24-08:00","id":321005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320876#post320876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awareness also contains the rediculous Wise Choice charm. For a small cost, you can know which choice (of any finite set you list) will lead to the best personal outcome for you! This has some obvious Paranoia uses: which path home should I take, should I get in the first carriage or the second one, should I trust Vizier Judas Starscream or not, etc. It can also be used to predict exactly who is going to try to assassinate you next (most useful if you know someone is gunning for you). Have a friend set up a betting pool, where people can guess names and whoever guesses right gets a prize. Then, get a bunch of tiles with letters on them, and assemble a name using Wise Choice (which tile should I place on the board next, given that I'm going to keep doing this until I get a complete name?) and then enter the result into the betting pool. Since the best outcome for you is both a) winning the bet and b) finding the assassin, the charm will give you the correct answer every time (barring cases where knowing your would-be killer is worse for you than not knowing, in which case you should be fine not knowing). Of course, this is an incredibly ineficient O(n) method that would drain motes like crazy, and only works for within the next month unless you exploit recursion, but I think optimizing information gains from Wise Choice is slightly outside the scope of this post.<br /> <br /> As a side note, you would be amazed at how much you can get done with Wise Choice and a grid map of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The image of, say, Vizier Judas Starscream playing ouija board with Fate amuses me immensely. Most things about the image of Vizier Judas Starscream amuse me immensely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:00:31-08:00","id":321007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320879#post320879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wife/son/secretary</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not want to mess with gender-swapped Athena if I were you, even if they do seem to have taken up slightly less glamorous work lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They&quot; is an excellent gender neutral pronoun.<br /> Avatar adapted from art by Cordell Felix <a href=\"http://cordellfelix.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cordellfelix.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":1177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1177-arrghus","user":"Arrghus","date":". 11-24-2014, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1177-arrghus","name":"Arrghus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:30:42-08:00","id":321028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrghus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=321007#post321007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not want to mess with gender-swapped Athena if I were you, even if they do seem to have taken up slightly less glamorous work lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, being a legendary demigod/shapeshifting killtruck/apocalypse prince does help for *surviving* those fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:37:18-08:00","id":321038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=321005#post321005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The image of, say, Vizier Judas Starscream playing ouija board with Fate amuses me immensely. Most things about the image of Vizier Judas Starscream amuse me immensely.</div> </div> </div> </div>How dare you impugn the Royal Vizier's good name? Judas only wants what's best for His Majesty and the kingdom. I'll admit the yellow snake eyes are a bit sinister-looking, but it's no more a cause for alarm than his goatee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T14:59:44-08:00","id":321072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320800#post320800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the developer comments on the Charm design seems to be following this logic and front running it; they're already speculating on the things Sidereals can do so they can design Charms representing Solars countering them, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that Charms are often likened to CCGs, but I'd really rather not bring in hard counters into Exalted. Being hard countered in a situation where there's nothing really at stake like a game of Magic is incredibly not fun, and I would extrapolate that it would suck the balls of seven different donkeys, at minimum, to pull that into RPGs.<br /> <br /> That and I thought it was generally consensus that things like Terrestial Charms failing against magic or that dumbass anti-Avoidance Kata spell in RotSE were things we were pretending didn't exist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T15:09:15-08:00","id":321078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320876#post320876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awareness also contains the rediculous Wise Choice charm. For a small cost, you can know which choice (of any finite set you list) will lead to the best personal outcome for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, Wise Choice not only selects the options you provide it, but according to the criteria you give it.<br /> <br /> If your priorities are mistaken or misaligned, then it won't help you. Like, if you ask &quot;which of these paths is the best one to take to get within face slapping distance of Malfeas&quot;, you won't get &quot;that's the worst idea ever&quot; as an answer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T15:13:48-08:00","id":321083,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being hard to pin down if they don't want to be pinned down&quot; is kind of a Sidereal schtick -- as antagonists, they're <i>supposed</i> to be like the one-armed man from the Fugitive, or the secret master villain who mainly works behind the scenes. I don't think I'd want that to go away, because it's a part of their appeal, but it'd be nice if their abilities were designed more with thought to how they might play out in that scenario when you're not the Sidereal. But, I mean, &quot;being one step ahead&quot; is pretty much where you want Sidereals to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320876#post320876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the best outcome for you is both a) winning the bet and b) finding the assassin, the charm will give you the correct answer every time (barring cases where knowing your would-be killer is worse for you than not knowing, in which case you should be fine not knowing). Of course, this is an incredibly ineficient O(n) method that would drain motes like crazy, and only works for within the next month unless you exploit recursion, but I think optimizing information gains from Wise Choice is slightly outside the scope of this post.<br /> <br /> As a side note, you would be amazed at how much you can get done with Wise Choice and a grid map of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wise Choice isn't <i>quite</i> this good, happily. The 2e version requires you to define what you consider the best outcome, which means you may end up optimizing for something unwise. Additionally, while the 2e version casts ahead up to a month and can be extended through teamwork, the 1e version just gives &quot;short-term results&quot;, which absent further instructions I would tend to interpret in the context of the choice. So either version can give you a very bad long-term outcome in exchange for a good short-term one -- especially problematic when the best short-term outcome isn't a clear winner.<br /> <br /> As a Sidereal, you can and should try to use it cleverly, but making it your one-size-fits-all solution for figuring things out will probably lead to more surprises than you might like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 11-24-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T16:14:34-08:00","id":321141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=321083#post321083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Being hard to pin down if they don't want to be pinned down&quot; is kind of a Sidereal schtick -- as antagonists, they're <i>supposed</i> to be like the one-armed man from the Fugitive, or the secret master villain who mainly works behind the scenes. I don't think I'd want that to go away, because it's a part of their appeal, but it'd be nice if their abilities were designed more with thought to how they might play out in that scenario when you're not the Sidereal. But, I mean, &quot;being one step ahead&quot; is pretty much where you want Sidereals to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also say there might be occasions in which seeing the danger coming doesn't quite help much, because the danger is still greater than anything you can actually bring to bear against it.<br /> <br /> At least you can set your affairs in order...<br /> <br /> People talk up Avoidance Kata, and it is pretty good, but it <i>was</i> written with a logical constraint; you can't be further away than you could have gotten in the time since the last juncture where you could have chosen to go somewhere else. I'm sure there have been more than a few Sidereals who encountered a Lunar hunting for them, declared &quot;I was never here&quot;, and then had to hope that it would give them a sufficient head-start on a Lunar who would realise that, no, the Sidereal isn't <i>here</i>, but by unmatched sight and smell and hearing I know for sure that they're over <i>there</i>, and sometimes it wasn't enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know that Charms are often likened to CCGs, but I'd really rather not bring in hard counters into Exalted. Being hard countered in a situation where there's nothing really at stake like a game of Magic is incredibly not fun, and I would extrapolate that it would suck the balls of seven different donkeys, at minimum, to pull that into RPGs.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> What do you take from the Ahlat vs Octavian playtest?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and I thought it was generally consensus that things like Terrestial Charms failing against magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrials failing against magic is bad because it's clunky and too all-encompassing.<br /> <br /> A Charm to, say, turn invisible having a logical (but not infallible) counter in terms of a Charm to greatly enhance hearing, or to notice incidental details like foot-shaped impressions in the ground, or to sense local deadly intent?<br /> <br /> It sounds better than alternatives like &quot;remove invisibility altogether&quot; or &quot;do nothing and hope people don't notice that invisibility makes you basically unstoppable&quot;.<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe it will provide a bit of context in which the failures of Sidereals are a matter of limitations and bad luck and enemies who managed to reasonably and intelligently overcome them rather than assumed incompetence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T02:27:07-08:00","id":321599,"title":"","content":"Getting caught off-guard or poisoned in Third Edition is bad but it's not the inescapable turd sandwich it was in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> As such charms, can afford to be more about turning the tables rather than shrugging everything off because if you don't then you'll die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T09:50:53-08:00","id":321891,"title":"","content":"When I saw the thread title, all I could think of was this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D-OGsSb0BPU\" data-code=\"D-OGsSb0BPU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/D-OGsSb0BPU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T10:11:24-08:00","id":321907,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would characterize the main constraint of Avoidance Kata as &quot;it is a form of emergency retreat&quot;, which means that using it a lot has the same downsides you'd expect of doing a lot of emergency retreating. <i>Not being there</i> is often a really significant drawback in itself, particularly for people as busy, regulated and infrastructure-bound as Sidereals, even before considering that the place you are instead is unpredictable and unplanned. AK is nice because once you realize that this nefarious psychic foresaw your arrival and slipped out in advance, and this is a thing they can do whenever because they're a nefarious psychic, the naive way you would handle that in character tends to also be an effective method to deal with Avoidance Kata from a mechanical standpoint.<br /> <br /> I think it could stand to have its limitations explained a bit more clearly, but AK isn't really what I'd call a &quot;problem&quot; charm, even from the angle that the character is an antagonist the PCs are chasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T08:30:01-08:00","id":322819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=320879#post320879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finding a way to threaten something that a given Sidereal will actually stay and fight for has traditionally been a good way of short-circuiting a lot of their tricks. Who cares if you can sense future danger or declare yourself absent from fights when I have my daiklave's edge to the throat of your wife/son/secretary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a tactic that also gets used BY Sidereals (and Deebs, for that matter) to pin down Lunars? I've always wondered how the Chosen of being anyone or anything at a moment's notice, with wings, gills, or just the power to outrun the wind itself, keep getting punked by Wyld Hunts, instead of vanishing into the wilderness or discreetly-eating one of their pursuers for even MORE mayhem-causing shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh god I didn't mean to invoke Meerkat-Steals-the-Spotlight Prana, this is just something that's been bugging me; please don't let it derail the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T08:34:26-08:00","id":322836,"title":"","content":"For the sake of contributing, this is actually how the PCs in my Abyssals game took down an Elder Sidereal - he was trying to set a trap for them anyhow, and in avoiding it they (and the party's two Moonshadows in particular) managed to flip him off SO HARD it sent him into Limit Break and he decided to go down swinging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T09:06:55-08:00","id":322854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=322819#post322819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered how the Chosen of being anyone or anything at a moment's notice, with wings, gills, or just the power to outrun the wind itself, keep getting punked by Wyld Hunts, instead of vanishing into the wilderness or discreetly-eating one of their pursuers for even MORE mayhem-causing shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you think you can win so you fight: sometimes you're right, sometimes you're wrong. Sometimes you're young and inexperienced and they get you before your power blossoms into something that can really resist. Sometimes you're overconfident; sometimes you get lazy; sometimes they have better intel.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Wyld Hunt isn't full of magic-wielding demigods too :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T09:14:22-08:00","id":322871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=322854#post322854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes you think you can win so you fight: sometimes you're right, sometimes you're wrong. Sometimes you're young and inexperienced and they get you before your power blossoms into something that can really resist. Sometimes you're overconfident; sometimes you get lazy; sometimes they have better intel.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Wyld Hunt isn't full of magic-wielding demigods too :P</div> </div> </div> </div>And sometimes your name is Sleeves <i>of War</i> for a reason, and you are not inclined do differently than face they head on (with your army)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T09:15:59-08:00","id":322874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=322871#post322871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sometimes your name is Sleeves <i>of War</i> for a reason, and you are not inclined do differently than face they head on (with your army)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nailed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T18:14:23-08:00","id":323307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=322819#post322819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a tactic that also gets used BY Sidereals (and Deebs, for that matter) to pin down Lunars? I've always wondered how the Chosen of being anyone or anything at a moment's notice, with wings, gills, or just the power to outrun the wind itself, keep getting punked by Wyld Hunts, instead of vanishing into the wilderness or discreetly-eating one of their pursuers for even MORE mayhem-causing shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Sidereals are more likely to take a reactive posture, waiting for Lunars to expose themselves by taking some proactive approach (note that prophecy lets Sidereals do some of the stuff usually classified as &quot;reaction&quot; before the original action has actually taken place). The time and energy it takes to track down a Lunar, identify something that matters them, and then threaten that thing are not insignificant, and even if everything goes exactly as planned you still end up on the wrong side of an enraged Lunar. It could be done, and I'm sure it is, but I don't think it's the most natural way for the Sidereals to approach that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T22:18:24-08:00","id":323426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=321141#post321141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you take from the Ahlat vs Octavian playtest?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A playtest occurred.&quot;<br /> <br /> I largely disregarded it because it didn't have any concrete information. Yes, Ahlat turned the tide on Octavian, but that may or may not have anything to do with the combat system. I've been in the D&amp;D game where the Strength 6 wizard is busting through doors like a boss while the three warriors are rolling so poorly couldn't toss a pixie, let alone bend any bars or lift any gates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Charm to, say, turn invisible having a logical (but not infallible) counter in terms of a Charm to greatly enhance hearing, or to notice incidental details like foot-shaped impressions in the ground, or to sense local deadly intent?] </div> </div> </div>Roight. That's a soft counter, and I have no objection to them. I don't want there to be <i>hard</i> counters. I don't want there to be &quot;If you're fighting against Dragon-Blooded, you always take these three Charms because there's fuck all they can do about them&quot; or &quot;This is explicitly your anti-Lunar Charm.&quot; Leave that shit to Magic and Starcraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T01:33:52-08:00","id":323521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323426#post323426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I largely disregarded it because it didn't have any concrete information. Yes, Ahlat turned the tide on Octavian, but that may or may not have anything to do with the combat system. I've been in the D&amp;D game where the Strength 6 wizard is busting through doors like a boss while the three warriors are rolling so poorly couldn't toss a pixie, let alone bend any bars or lift any gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still contains terminology articulating the concept of Charms countering other Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a soft counter, and I have no objection to them. I don't want there to be <i>hard</i> counters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction seems largely arbitrary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T01:38:26-08:00","id":323523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323426#post323426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;A playtest occurred.&quot;<br /> <br /> I largely disregarded it because it didn't have any concrete information. Yes, Ahlat turned the tide on Octavian, but that may or may not have anything to do with the combat system. I've been in the D&amp;D game where the Strength 6 wizard is busting through doors like a boss while the three warriors are rolling so poorly couldn't toss a pixie, let alone bend any bars or lift any gates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Roight. That's a soft counter, and I have no objection to them. I don't want there to be <i>hard</i> counters. I don't want there to be &quot;If you're fighting against Dragon-Blooded, you always take these three Charms because there's fuck all they can do about them&quot; or &quot;This is explicitly your anti-Lunar Charm.&quot; Leave that shit to Magic and Starcraft.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Magic has *also* moved away from hard-counters; instead of &quot;this is my anti-blue card&quot; you now tend to get &quot;this card is usually pretty good at slowing down people trying to blitz you with a ton of small guys&quot; or whatever... precisely because it's more interesting that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T06:34:33-08:00","id":323600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323521#post323521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction seems largely arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it completely isn't. A soft counter can be played around with enough skill, luck and favor of the gods. It makes any sort of competitive endeavor more interesting because it puts the results in doubt while not declaring a winner as soon as one is used.<br /> <br /> A hard counter, on the other hand, is much more difficult to integrate into any sort of competitive field without making it a dull slog to play (and in some cases, watch). Starcraft can get any with having hard counters because <i>everyone</i> has hard counters, and it's fairly easy to build around them (someone hard countered your hydralisks? Build mutalisks instead).<br /> <br /> One guess as to who had the vast majority of hard counters in 1e and 2e Exalted. In fact, Judge's Ear Technique has been specifically cited as being shit for stories because of its hard counter nature, even if that precise language wasn't used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323523#post323523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic has *also* moved away from hard-counters; instead of &quot;this is my anti-blue card&quot; you now tend to get &quot;this card is usually pretty good at slowing down people trying to blitz you with a ton of small guys&quot; or whatever... precisely because it's more interesting that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. I've sorta-kinda-maybe looked at Magic again in recent months, but I haven't looked at the compeittive scene at all. That sounds neat, though...I imagine the meta is <i>much</i> more interesting than when I played seriously.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:59:21-08:00","id":323632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323521#post323521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction seems largely arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction is not even remotely arbitrary.<br /> <br /> A hard counter is like <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=382897\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. You push a button and whatever your opponent was doing, it is foiled. Playing large, expensive cards becomes functionally impossible because playing a large card will always be responded to with Counterspell. Judge's Ear Technique is a hard counter: you make it impossible to do anything involving lying and your opponent has no practical way of defeating this. Dragonblooded Charms failing against magic is another hard counter: there is no way to get around it with planning or luck, just suddenly none of your applicable Charms work. Even if Charms were not as foundational to your character as they are, this would still be poor design because it declares the outcome in advance.<br /> <br /> A soft counter is like <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=292750\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. When you play Force Spike, your opponent has two options. They can either choose to let you counter the card you used it on, which will leave you down 1 mana and the Force Spike card and them down the mana cost of the card as well as the card itself, or they can choose to pay an additional mana, which will leave you down 1 mana and the Force Spike and them down the mana cost of the card +1. There are situations in which either one might be a preferable outcome, such as if they have a stronger card coming up on the same turn and they need all of their remaining mana to play it. In general, Force Spike makes it more expensive for your opponent to use single large cards against you, but does very little to thwart an attack based around using lots of small creatures. There are <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=280232\" target=\"_blank\">other soft counters</a> to deal with that kind of attack that don't do much to hinder single large cards. More importantly, Force Spike makes strategies built around large creatures require more foresight from your opponent - leaving a bit of mana in reserve in case you play it, for instance - but it does not make such strategies <i>impossible</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","user":"Couch","date":". 11-27-2014, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:30:17-08:00","id":323643,"title":"","content":"I want to preface by saying that Solars and Sidereals are both constantly fighting for the place of my favorite Exalt, for pretty much opposite reasons. I love Solars as the shining hero who shapes the world through bold words and deeds just as much as I love Sidereals as the FBI/KGB/CIA agent of heaven who shapes the world with secrets and subtlety.<br /> <br /> With that said, I believe that Solars having a hard counter to Sidereal shenanigans makes a degree of sense from a narrative standpoint. When you get fate and destiny involved in a fantasy setting, there are usually two outcomes: Either the hero is guided by fate to fulfill his ultimate purpose, or the hero subverts fate to write his own destiny.<br /> <br /> Sidereals, being agents of fate (and also it's master) fall in the former category. They are guided by Fate in the form of their charms towards success in whatever goal they choose. Solars on the other hand are in for latter category. They shrug of the threads of fate and ignore destiny to pick their own path in life.<br /> <br /> Given the usual conventions of the hero/fate narrative, it makes a degree of sense that Solars, being the Heroic Archetype Exalted, have some hard counters against some Sidereal powers, who are the Agents of Fate Exalted. This isn't to say that Solars should be able to no-sell ALL of a Sidereal's spiffy powers. The struggle of the hero vs his destiny (as assigned by the Sidereal) is also a common plot. I suspect that Solars will have hard counters to the more overt examples of what I affectionally refer to as the Sidereal's cheaty bullshit fate powers, which will represent the Solar's ability to define their own fate. At the same time, Sidereals will still have a number of options to force the Solar to conform to the fate the Sidereal picks and chooses.<br /> <br /> Tl;DR: I believe Solars will be able to hard counter some Sidereal abilities, but I think this is unlikely to invalidate the Sidereal's ability to do the cheaty fate bullshit that I love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 11-27-2014, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:33:33-08:00","id":323645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323600#post323600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool. I've sorta-kinda-maybe looked at Magic again in recent months, but I haven't looked at the compeittive scene at all. That sounds neat, though...I imagine the meta is <i>much</i> more interesting than when I played seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Welcome to competitive Magic, you can choose between two decks: Artifact Affinity, and Deck Designed To Counter Artifact Affinity.&quot;<br /> &quot;fuck this hobby&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:51:01-08:00","id":323650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323643#post323643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tl;DR: I believe Solars will be able to hard counter some Sidereal abilities, but I think this is unlikely to invalidate the Sidereal's ability to do the cheaty fate bullshit that I love.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game implemented hard counters for a long, long time. Cheap perfects, DB magic failing to Celestial magic, Keyword defenses ESPECIALLY Shaping (when you have a cheap longterm Shaping defense and 90% of deleterious effects get tagged as Shaping be Dumbass Reasons), the JB roll automatically superseding social tension, Judge's Ear...<br /> <br /> These hard counters largely sucked, even if they had reasons for existing (those reasons being even more fundamental system flaws - those flaws explain the reason for nope.jpg but don't justify it, since those flaws never had to be created as system assumptions from the get go, yet they were).<br /> <br /> The current authors agree that hard counters largely sucked.<br /> <br /> So some people here think the authors are going to add in even more hard counters? Or are hoping they do?<br /> <br /> What the christ? Learn from past mistakes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:57:58-08:00","id":323655,"title":"","content":"I believe that few types of system mechanics, such as hard counters, are inherently bad. Rather it has to do with how they are implemented. Hard counters have their place in Exalted, but should only be employed in ways that supplement player agency and facilitate fun. I believe the Devs actually have talked about giving Solars hard counters to Sidereal abilities. Assuming this is the case, I doubt that these will be harmful to playing a Sidereal in any significant way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:08:08-08:00","id":323658,"title":"","content":"I just prefer having to make tradeoff choices to nope.jpg. The fact that one can no longer easily be one-shot on Turn 1 in 3e allows players to make real choices regarding their combat resources versus having a need to spam a paranoia Combo as their only Charm exertion every turn to avoid getting 1-shot. And to me that's a good thing. <br /> <br /> I don't think hard counters are inherently bad in all systems; as was said, in RTS games a hard counter isn't the worst because everyone has hard counters; comparatively, in Magic, it can be a pain/problematic from a fun perspective because it can set up a deck to automatically have little chance of success from the get go.<br /> <br /> I think they're pretty bad in RPGs just given how they can trivially shut down challenges. Again, Judge's Ear comes to mind. Integrity becoming such a kitchen sink that somehow your destiny was proprietary and not getting a +1 TN to particular rolls because of Astrology deserved the same Keyword protection as not being morphed into a lava lamp carrot in the Wyld. Because to some writers, the two were equally as bad for Solars to have to put up with.<br /> <br /> The big problem with Solars having hard counters to Sidereals is that in a Solar game, you can trivially overcome the powers of a Sidereal foe, and in a Sidereal game your powers will be much less useful against a Solar villain. Neither of these situations leads to particularly interesting gaming; needing to find a way around your foe's defenses or needing to be clever in a way to deflect their attacks is always more engaging to me than having a NOPE button. I don't see how that isn't harmful to playing a Sidereal, or to trying to run a Sidereal as an enemy of a group of Solar PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:53:52-08:00","id":323695,"title":"","content":"There's nothing intrinsically bad about hard counters. It's just that they need to come with significant costs, either opportunity costs or explicit resource costs, that are sufficient to ensure that you can be punished for using them. The problem with traditional perfects was that there wasn't really anything going on except mote/WP economy in most cases, so there was not a large tactical element to using them -- unless your opponent(s) collectively had vastly more motes/WP than you, you just had to figure out in a general sense whether the thing being perfected cost more than the perfect.<br /> <br /> I haven't played Magic in a million years, but I remember Counterspell being pretty interesting. &quot;Two islands untapped&quot; was one of the most engaging mind games, because a) it might be a bluff, b) you only get to counter one thing per turn, and c) Keeping two islands untapped all the time for pressure put you way behind in the curve. It was by far the most tactical thing going on with early Blue, since you had threat, guessing games, and valuation traps going on. So hard counters can absolutely work well -- it's just that they require careful calibration, because their failure state is totally binary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:57:18-08:00","id":323807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323695#post323695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing intrinsically bad about hard counters. It's just that they need to come with significant costs, either opportunity costs or explicit resource costs, that are sufficient to ensure that you can be punished for using them. The problem with traditional perfects was that there wasn't really anything going on except mote/WP economy in most cases, so there was not a large tactical element to using them -- unless your opponent(s) collectively had vastly more motes/WP than you, you just had to figure out in a general sense whether the thing being perfected cost more than the perfect.<br /> <br /> I haven't played Magic in a million years, but I remember Counterspell being pretty interesting. &quot;Two islands untapped&quot; was one of the most engaging mind games, because a) it might be a bluff, b) you only get to counter one thing per turn, and c) Keeping two islands untapped all the time for pressure put you way behind in the curve. It was by far the most tactical thing going on with early Blue, since you had threat, guessing games, and valuation traps going on. So hard counters can absolutely work well -- it's just that they require careful calibration, because their failure state is totally binary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the most tactical thing going on with early Blue, but early Magic was in many ways primitive compared to the modern version of the game, and there's a reason they almost never reprint Counterspell anymore. Later versions like Force Spike are much more tactically engaging, because they have much more nuance in how they resolve which creates more options for both parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T18:09:03-08:00","id":324024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/320767-i-see-dead-peop-i-mean-the-future-about-high-awareness-sidereal?p=323807#post323807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was the most tactical thing going on with early Blue, but early Magic was in many ways primitive compared to the modern version of the game, and there's a reason they almost never reprint Counterspell anymore. Later versions like Force Spike are much more tactically engaging, because they have much more nuance in how they resolve which creates more options for both parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's so much a statement about soft counters being tactically superior to hard counters <i>in general</i> as it is about the curve being the lord your god, and anything that fucks with it being incredibly powerful.<br /> <br /> (The funniest hard counters from the early CCG era were Decipher Star Wars' &quot;magic bullets&quot;. They had vowed never to ban cards so whenever something turned out to be OP they would introduce a hard counter in the next set that trashed <i>that specific card</i><i> by name</i>. Good times.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 11-27-2014, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}